deployment_preface.sh|43|25|Deployment|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|The release manager is deliberately self-sufficient. It always carries a small|deployment_preface.sh:::Deployment:
deployment_preface.sh|44|26|Deployment|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|standalone UI and default-theme fallback so it can bootstrap a clean machine or|deployment_preface.sh:::Deployment:
deployment_preface.sh|45|27|Deployment|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|recover a damaged installation. When a healthy SolidGroundUX framework is available|deployment_preface.sh:::Deployment:
deployment_preface.sh|46|28|Deployment|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|at the selected target root, the manager may reuse the normal framework UI primitives|deployment_preface.sh:::Deployment:
