deployment_preface.sh|76|58|Release Preparation|Deployment||normal|||L2Sectionbody|The normal manifest describes the paths contained in the release.|deployment_preface.sh::Deployment:Release Preparation:
deployment_preface.sh|77|59|Release Preparation|Deployment||normal|||L2Sectionbody||deployment_preface.sh::Deployment:Release Preparation:
deployment_preface.sh|78|60|Release Preparation|Deployment||normal|||L2Sectionbody|The removed manifest is generated by comparing the previous release manifest with|deployment_preface.sh::Deployment:Release Preparation:
deployment_preface.sh|79|61|Release Preparation|Deployment||normal|||L2Sectionbody|the new one. It contains paths that existed in the previous release but no longer|deployment_preface.sh::Deployment:Release Preparation:
deployment_preface.sh|80|62|Release Preparation|Deployment||normal|||L2Sectionbody|belong to the new release. release-manager.sh applies this file during an update.|deployment_preface.sh::Deployment:Release Preparation:
