deployment_preface.sh|113|95|Release Manager|Deployment||normal|||L2Sectionbody|    /var/lib/solidgroundux/projects/<project>/archive/<release>|deployment_preface.sh::Deployment:Release Manager:
deployment_preface.sh|114|96|Release Manager|Deployment||normal|||L2Sectionbody||deployment_preface.sh::Deployment:Release Manager:
deployment_preface.sh|115|97|Release Manager|Deployment||normal|||L2Sectionbody|The highest versioned archive directory represents the currently installed release|deployment_preface.sh::Deployment:Release Manager:
deployment_preface.sh|116|98|Release Manager|Deployment||normal|||L2Sectionbody|for that project. No separate current-version database is required.|deployment_preface.sh::Deployment:Release Manager:
deployment_preface.sh|117|99|Release Manager|Deployment||normal|||L2Sectionbody||deployment_preface.sh::Deployment:Release Manager:
deployment_preface.sh|118|100|Release Manager|Deployment||normal|||L2Sectionbody|A first install consists of validating and extracting a complete release archive.|deployment_preface.sh::Deployment:Release Manager:
deployment_preface.sh|119|101|Release Manager|Deployment||normal|||L2Sectionbody||deployment_preface.sh::Deployment:Release Manager:
deployment_preface.sh|120|102|Release Manager|Deployment||normal|||L2Sectionbody|A later install is treated as an update. The new release is extracted normally,|deployment_preface.sh::Deployment:Release Manager:
deployment_preface.sh|121|103|Release Manager|Deployment||normal|||L2Sectionbody|and its .removed manifest is applied so files that disappeared from the release|deployment_preface.sh::Deployment:Release Manager:
deployment_preface.sh|122|104|Release Manager|Deployment||normal|||L2Sectionbody|are removed from the active installation.|deployment_preface.sh::Deployment:Release Manager:
deployment_preface.sh|123|105|Release Manager|Deployment||normal|||L2Sectionbody||deployment_preface.sh::Deployment:Release Manager:
deployment_preface.sh|124|106|Release Manager|Deployment||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Rollback installs a selected archived release again and removes files that belong|deployment_preface.sh::Deployment:Release Manager:
deployment_preface.sh|125|107|Release Manager|Deployment||normal|||L2Sectionbody|only to the newer release. Newer archived releases are returned to releases/ so|deployment_preface.sh::Deployment:Release Manager:
deployment_preface.sh|126|108|Release Manager|Deployment||normal|||L2Sectionbody|the highest remaining archive directory continues to represent the active version.|deployment_preface.sh::Deployment:Release Manager:
deployment_preface.sh|127|109|Release Manager|Deployment||normal|||L2Sectionbody||deployment_preface.sh::Deployment:Release Manager:
deployment_preface.sh|128|110|Release Manager|Deployment||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Removal removes the active release contents and returns archived release sets to|deployment_preface.sh::Deployment:Release Manager:
deployment_preface.sh|129|111|Release Manager|Deployment||normal|||L2Sectionbody|releases/, preserving them for later reinstallation.|deployment_preface.sh::Deployment:Release Manager:
deployment_preface.sh|130|112|Release Manager|Deployment||normal|||L2Sectionbody||deployment_preface.sh::Deployment:Release Manager:
