deploy-workspace.sh|14|2||||label|||modulebody|Description|deploy-workspace.sh::::
deploy-workspace.sh|15|3||||normal|||modulebody|  Collects deployment settings from command-line arguments and interactive prompts,|deploy-workspace.sh::::
deploy-workspace.sh|16|4||||normal|||modulebody|  resolves the requested workspace files into a concrete relative path list, creates|deploy-workspace.sh::::
deploy-workspace.sh|17|5||||normal|||modulebody|  a tar stream, and passes that stream to receive-files.sh locally or over SSH.|deploy-workspace.sh::::
deploy-workspace.sh|18|6||||normal|||modulebody||deploy-workspace.sh::::
deploy-workspace.sh|19|7||||label|||modulebody|Design principles|deploy-workspace.sh::::
deploy-workspace.sh|20|8||||normal|||modulebody|  - Selection and transport remain separate from destination-side installation policy|deploy-workspace.sh::::
deploy-workspace.sh|21|9||||normal|||modulebody|  - Local and remote deployment use the same receive-files.sh contract|deploy-workspace.sh::::
deploy-workspace.sh|22|10||||normal|||modulebody|  - Command-line values override saved defaults|deploy-workspace.sh::::
deploy-workspace.sh|23|11||||normal|||modulebody|  - Confirmed deployment settings are always saved; the success timestamp changes only after a successful receive operation|deploy-workspace.sh::::
deploy-workspace.sh|24|12||||normal|||modulebody|  - Changed-after defaults to the last successful deployment timestamp when available|deploy-workspace.sh::::
