doc-generator.sh|24|11||||label|||modulebody|Design principles|doc-generator.sh::::
doc-generator.sh|25|12||||normal|||modulebody|  - Collection logic is kept separate from rendering logic|doc-generator.sh::::
doc-generator.sh|26|13||||normal|||modulebody|  - Script behavior is deterministic and state-aware|doc-generator.sh::::
doc-generator.sh|27|14||||normal|||modulebody|  - Framework conventions are reused wherever possible|doc-generator.sh::::
doc-generator.sh|28|15||||normal|||modulebody|  - Interactive prompting remains optional rather than mandatory|doc-generator.sh::::
doc-generator.sh|29|16||||normal|||modulebody||doc-generator.sh::::
doc-generator.sh|30|17||||label|||modulebody|Role in framework|doc-generator.sh::::
doc-generator.sh|31|18||||normal|||modulebody|  - Executable entry point for documentation collection workflows|doc-generator.sh::::
doc-generator.sh|32|19||||normal|||modulebody|  - Demonstrates canonical integration with sgnd-bootstrap and common libraries|doc-generator.sh::::
doc-generator.sh|33|20||||normal|||modulebody|  - Bridges bootstrap, state, argument parsing, and collector execution|doc-generator.sh::::
doc-generator.sh|34|21||||normal|||modulebody||doc-generator.sh::::
