receive-files.sh|3|1||||normal|||moduleheader|SolidGroundUX - Receive Files|receive-files.sh::::
receive-files.sh|14|2||||label|||modulebody|Description|receive-files.sh::::
receive-files.sh|15|3||||normal|||modulebody|  Receives a tar archive through standard input, validates that every archive entry|receive-files.sh::::
receive-files.sh|16|4||||normal|||modulebody|  is a safe relative path, and extracts the streamed workspace files beneath the|receive-files.sh::::
receive-files.sh|17|5||||normal|||modulebody|  requested target root.|receive-files.sh::::
receive-files.sh|18|6||||normal|||modulebody||receive-files.sh::::
receive-files.sh|19|7||||label|||modulebody|Design principles|receive-files.sh::::
receive-files.sh|20|8||||normal|||modulebody|  - File selection remains the responsibility of deploy-workspace.sh|receive-files.sh::::
receive-files.sh|21|9||||normal|||modulebody|  - Archive entries always remain relative to the supplied target root|receive-files.sh::::
