doc-processor.sh|2|1||||normal|||moduleheader|SolidGroundUX - Document processor|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|15|2||||label|||modulebody|Description|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|16|3||||normal|||modulebody|  Provides the core parsing engine for the SolidGroundUX documentation system.|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|17|4||||normal|||modulebody||doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|18|5||||label|||modulebody|The processor|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|19|6||||normal|||modulebody|    - Iterates source files line-by-line|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|20|7||||normal|||modulebody|    - Interprets structured comment conventions (headers, metadata, sections, items)|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|21|8||||normal|||modulebody|    - Maintains parsing state (header, section hierarchy, current item, etc.)|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|22|9||||normal|||modulebody|    - Normalizes detected elements into a flat render stream (DOC_CONTENT_LINES)|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|23|10||||normal|||modulebody||doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|24|11||||normal|||modulebody|  Parsing is convention-based and deterministic. Each recognized line contributes|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|25|12||||normal|||modulebody|  either state transitions or a normalized documentation record.|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|26|13||||normal|||modulebody||doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|27|14||||label|||modulebody|Design principles|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|28|15||||normal|||modulebody|  - Single-pass parsing (no backtracking or multi-phase analysis)|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|29|16||||label|||modulebody|- Separation of concerns|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|30|17||||normal|||modulebody|      * Detection/state mutation|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|31|18||||normal|||modulebody|      * Content normalization|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|32|19||||normal|||modulebody|      * Rendering (handled elsewhere)|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|33|20||||normal|||modulebody|  - Convention over configuration (strict comment grammar)|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|34|21||||normal|||modulebody|  - Minimal side effects outside controlled doc_* and mod_* variables|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|35|22||||normal|||modulebody|  - Transparent state transitions for debuggability|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|36|23||||normal|||modulebody||doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|37|24||||label|||modulebody|Role in framework|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|38|25||||normal|||modulebody|  - Core documentation data collector|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|39|26||||normal|||modulebody|  - Produces the canonical DOC_CONTENT_LINES dataset consumed by renderers|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|40|27||||normal|||modulebody|  - Bridges raw source code and higher-level documentation output (HTML, etc.)|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|41|28||||normal|||modulebody|  - Shared parsing engine for all documentation-related tooling|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|42|29||||normal|||modulebody||doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|43|30||||label|||modulebody|Non-goals|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|44|31||||normal|||modulebody|  - Rendering output formats (HTML, Markdown, PDF, etc.)|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|45|32||||normal|||modulebody|  - Parsing arbitrary or free-form comments|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|46|33||||normal|||modulebody|  - Semantic analysis of code (only structured comment interpretation)|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|47|34||||normal|||modulebody|  - Cross-file linking or indexing logic|doc-processor.sh::::
doc-processor.sh|48|35||||normal|||modulebody||doc-processor.sh::::
