ui-say.sh|2|1||||normal|||moduleheader|SolidGroundUX - UI Messaging|ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|13|2||||label|||modulebody|Description|ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|14|3||||normal|||modulebody|  Implements consistent message output helpers for console applications.|ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|15|4||||normal|||modulebody||ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|16|5||||label|||modulebody|The library|ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|17|6||||normal|||modulebody|    - Provides a unified message API via `say` and typed wrappers (info, ok, warn, etc.)|ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|18|7||||normal|||modulebody|    - Applies consistent formatting, prefixes, and optional colorization|ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|19|8||||normal|||modulebody|    - Supports console output control via verbosity, debug flags, and message-type filtering|ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|20|9||||normal|||modulebody|    - Ensures all messages follow a unified visual and structural style|ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|21|10||||normal|||modulebody|    - Optionally performs best-effort file logging when enabled|ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|22|11||||normal|||modulebody||ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|23|12||||label|||modulebody|Design principles|ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|24|13||||normal|||modulebody|  - Consistent message semantics across all scripts|ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|25|14||||normal|||modulebody|  - Separation of message intent (type) from rendering and output policy|ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|26|15||||normal|||modulebody|  - Respect the framework log-level policy consistently|ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|27|16||||normal|||modulebody|  - Keep output predictable and script-friendly|ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|28|17||||normal|||modulebody||ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|29|18||||label|||modulebody|Role in framework|ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|30|19||||normal|||modulebody|  - Core messaging layer used by all SolidGroundUX scripts|ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|31|20||||normal|||modulebody|  - Serves as the primary mechanism for user-facing output and diagnostics|ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|32|21||||normal|||modulebody|  - Works alongside ui.sh for rendering and formatting|ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|33|22||||normal|||modulebody||ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|34|23||||label|||modulebody|Non-goals|ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|35|24||||normal|||modulebody|  - Persistent logging frameworks or advanced log management|ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|36|25||||normal|||modulebody|  - Complex formatting beyond message-level styling|ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|37|26||||normal|||modulebody|  - Replacement for dedicated logging systems|ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|38|27||||normal|||modulebody||ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|39|28||||label|||modulebody|Notes|ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|40|29||||normal|||modulebody|  - Console output is governed by SGND_CONSOLE_LOG_LEVEL; file output is governed by SGND_FILE_LOG_LEVEL.|ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|41|30||||normal|||modulebody|  - File logging is optional and best-effort; failures do not affect execution.|ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|42|31||||normal|||modulebody|  - Logfile writing is independent from console visibility.|ui-say.sh::::
ui-say.sh|43|32||||normal|||modulebody||ui-say.sh::::
