common core_preface.sh|27|8|Configuration Management|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionheader|Configuration Management|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Configuration Management:
common core_preface.sh|28|9|Configuration Management|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody| |common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Configuration Management:
common core_preface.sh|29|10|Configuration Management|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|The configuration subsystem provides a consistent mechanism for loading,|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Configuration Management:
common core_preface.sh|30|11|Configuration Management|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|validating, modifying, and persisting application settings.|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Configuration Management:
common core_preface.sh|31|12|Configuration Management|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody| |common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Configuration Management:
common core_preface.sh|32|13|Configuration Management|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Configuration values typically represent user preferences or application|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Configuration Management:
common core_preface.sh|33|14|Configuration Management|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|settings that remain relatively static between executions.|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Configuration Management:
common core_preface.sh|34|15|Configuration Management|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody| |common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Configuration Management:
common core_preface.sh|35|16|State Management|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionheader|State Management|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:State Management:
common core_preface.sh|36|17|State Management|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody| |common core_preface.sh::Available Services:State Management:
common core_preface.sh|37|18|State Management|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|The state subsystem stores runtime information that applications may wish to|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:State Management:
common core_preface.sh|38|19|State Management|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|remember between executions.|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:State Management:
common core_preface.sh|39|20|State Management|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody| |common core_preface.sh::Available Services:State Management:
common core_preface.sh|40|21|State Management|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Unlike configuration values, state represents remembered runtime choices and|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:State Management:
common core_preface.sh|41|22|State Management|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|workflow context such as previous selections, recently used values, UI choices,|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:State Management:
common core_preface.sh|42|23|State Management|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|or cached information. Scripts opt individual values into persistence explicitly.|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:State Management:
common core_preface.sh|43|24|State Management|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody| |common core_preface.sh::Available Services:State Management:
common core_preface.sh|44|25|Command-Line Arguments|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionheader|Command-Line Arguments|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Command-Line Arguments:
common core_preface.sh|45|26|Command-Line Arguments|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody| |common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Command-Line Arguments:
common core_preface.sh|46|27|Command-Line Arguments|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|The argument subsystem provides standardized command-line processing. After the|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Command-Line Arguments:
common core_preface.sh|47|28|Command-Line Arguments|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|bootstrap separates framework options from script arguments, applications can|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Command-Line Arguments:
common core_preface.sh|48|29|Command-Line Arguments|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|define their own declarative argument specification while retaining framework|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Command-Line Arguments:
common core_preface.sh|49|30|Command-Line Arguments|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|built-ins such as help, version reporting, tracing, debugging, and configuration|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Command-Line Arguments:
common core_preface.sh|50|31|Command-Line Arguments|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|overrides.|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Command-Line Arguments:
common core_preface.sh|51|32|Command-Line Arguments|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody||common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Command-Line Arguments:
common core_preface.sh|52|33|User Interface Services|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionheader|User Interface Services|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:User Interface Services:
common core_preface.sh|53|34|User Interface Services|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody||common core_preface.sh::Available Services:User Interface Services:
common core_preface.sh|54|35|User Interface Services|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|The UI subsystem provides a collection of functions intended to simplify|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:User Interface Services:
common core_preface.sh|55|36|User Interface Services|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|communication with the user.|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:User Interface Services:
common core_preface.sh|56|37|User Interface Services|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  |common core_preface.sh::Available Services:User Interface Services:
common core_preface.sh|57|38|User Interface Services|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Common operations such as informational messages, warnings, errors,|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:User Interface Services:
common core_preface.sh|58|39|User Interface Services|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|confirmations, prompts, selections, and formatted output are provided through|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:User Interface Services:
common core_preface.sh|59|40|User Interface Services|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|a consistent interface.|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:User Interface Services:
common core_preface.sh|60|41|User Interface Services|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody||common core_preface.sh::Available Services:User Interface Services:
common core_preface.sh|61|42|Console Applications|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionheader|Console Applications|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Console Applications:
common core_preface.sh|62|43|Console Applications|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody||common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Console Applications:
common core_preface.sh|63|44|Console Applications|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|`sgnd-menu.sh` provides a reusable public menu service independent of the SolidGround|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Console Applications:
common core_preface.sh|64|45|Console Applications|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Management Console host. Applications can create menu models, register groups and|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Console Applications:
common core_preface.sh|65|46|Console Applications|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|items, render pages, read selections, and dispatch registered actions through the|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Console Applications:
common core_preface.sh|66|47|Console Applications|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|public `sgnd_menu_*` API.|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Console Applications:
common core_preface.sh|67|48|Console Applications|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody||common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Console Applications:
common core_preface.sh|68|49|Console Applications|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|The Management Console is one consumer of that API. Its page modules are discovered|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Console Applications:
common core_preface.sh|69|50|Console Applications|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|from lightweight metadata and sourced lazily when first opened.|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Console Applications:
common core_preface.sh|70|51|Console Applications|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody||common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Console Applications:
common core_preface.sh|71|52|Documentation Generation|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionheader|Documentation Generation|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Documentation Generation:
common core_preface.sh|72|53|Documentation Generation|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody||common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Documentation Generation:
common core_preface.sh|73|54|Documentation Generation|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|The documentation generator extracts documentation directly from source files.|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Documentation Generation:
common core_preface.sh|74|55|Documentation Generation|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  |common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Documentation Generation:
common core_preface.sh|75|56|Documentation Generation|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Product information, architecture descriptions, API documentation, appendices,|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Documentation Generation:
common core_preface.sh|76|57|Documentation Generation|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|glossaries, and implementation notes are all maintained close to the source|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Documentation Generation:
common core_preface.sh|77|58|Documentation Generation|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|code and transformed into a navigable HTML documentation set.|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Documentation Generation:
common core_preface.sh|78|59|Documentation Generation|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody| |common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Documentation Generation:
common core_preface.sh|79|60|Documentation Generation|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|This approach helps ensure that documentation remains synchronized with the|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Documentation Generation:
common core_preface.sh|80|61|Documentation Generation|Available Services||normal|||L2Sectionbody|implementation and reduces the risk of documentation becoming outdated.|common core_preface.sh::Available Services:Documentation Generation:
sgnd-info.sh|2|1||||normal|||moduleheader|SolidGroundUX - Framework Information|sgnd-info.sh::::
sgnd-info.sh|13|2||||label|||modulebody|Description|sgnd-info.sh::::
sgnd-info.sh|14|3||||normal|||modulebody|  Exposes information about the SolidGroundUX framework and runtime environment.|sgnd-info.sh::::
sgnd-info.sh|15|4||||normal|||modulebody||sgnd-info.sh::::
sgnd-info.sh|16|5||||label|||modulebody|The library|sgnd-info.sh::::
sgnd-info.sh|17|6||||normal|||modulebody|    - Provides access to framework identity (name, version, paths)|sgnd-info.sh::::
sgnd-info.sh|18|7||||normal|||modulebody|    - Exposes resolved bootstrap values such as SGND_FRAMEWORK_ROOT and runtime paths|sgnd-info.sh::::
sgnd-info.sh|19|8||||normal|||modulebody|    - Supplies helper functions for displaying framework and environment details|sgnd-info.sh::::
sgnd-info.sh|20|9||||normal|||modulebody|    - Supports diagnostics, logging, and informational output|sgnd-info.sh::::
sgnd-info.sh|21|10||||normal|||modulebody||sgnd-info.sh::::
sgnd-info.sh|22|11||||label|||modulebody|Design principles|sgnd-info.sh::::
sgnd-info.sh|23|12||||normal|||modulebody|  - Keep information access centralized and consistent|sgnd-info.sh::::
sgnd-info.sh|24|13||||normal|||modulebody|  - Avoid duplication of framework identity data across modules|sgnd-info.sh::::
sgnd-info.sh|25|14||||normal|||modulebody|  - Ensure values reflect the active runtime environment|sgnd-info.sh::::
sgnd-info.sh|26|15||||normal|||modulebody|  - Keep implementation lightweight and dependency-free where possible|sgnd-info.sh::::
sgnd-info.sh|27|16||||normal|||modulebody||sgnd-info.sh::::
sgnd-info.sh|28|17||||label|||modulebody|Role in framework|sgnd-info.sh::::
sgnd-info.sh|29|18||||normal|||modulebody|  - Provides introspection capabilities for scripts and tools|sgnd-info.sh::::
sgnd-info.sh|30|19||||normal|||modulebody|  - Supports diagnostics, debugging, and informational commands|sgnd-info.sh::::
sgnd-info.sh|31|20||||normal|||modulebody|  - Complements bootstrap and configuration modules|sgnd-info.sh::::
sgnd-info.sh|32|21||||normal|||modulebody||sgnd-info.sh::::
sgnd-info.sh|33|22||||label|||modulebody|Non-goals|sgnd-info.sh::::
sgnd-info.sh|34|23||||normal|||modulebody|  - Configuration management (handled by cfg.sh)|sgnd-info.sh::::
sgnd-info.sh|35|24||||normal|||modulebody|  - Argument parsing or user interaction|sgnd-info.sh::::
sgnd-info.sh|36|25||||normal|||modulebody|  - Persistent state tracking|sgnd-info.sh::::
sgnd-info.sh|37|26||||normal|||modulebody||sgnd-info.sh::::
