bootstrap_preface.sh|2|1||||normal|||moduleheader|SolidGroundUX - Bootstrap Sequence|bootstrap_preface.sh::::
bootstrap_preface.sh|20|2|Bootstrap|||normal|||L1Sectionheader|Bootstrap|bootstrap_preface.sh:::Bootstrap:
bootstrap_preface.sh|21|3|Bootstrap|||normal|||L1Sectionbody||bootstrap_preface.sh:::Bootstrap:
bootstrap_preface.sh|22|4|Bootstrap|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|The bootstrap layer is the foundation of the SolidGroundUX runtime model.|bootstrap_preface.sh:::Bootstrap:
bootstrap_preface.sh|23|5|Bootstrap|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|  |bootstrap_preface.sh:::Bootstrap:
bootstrap_preface.sh|24|6|Bootstrap|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|Its purpose is to give executable scripts and reusable libraries a predictable|bootstrap_preface.sh:::Bootstrap:
bootstrap_preface.sh|25|7|Bootstrap|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|starting point before application-specific logic begins. It resolves framework|bootstrap_preface.sh:::Bootstrap:
bootstrap_preface.sh|26|8|Bootstrap|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|locations, initializes common globals, loads requested libraries, prepares|bootstrap_preface.sh:::Bootstrap:
bootstrap_preface.sh|27|9|Bootstrap|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|configuration handling, and registers the framework's built-in command-line|bootstrap_preface.sh:::Bootstrap:
