bootstrap_preface.sh|85|67|Global Definitions|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|The bootstrap process also prepares common SolidGroundUX global variables.|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Global Definitions:
bootstrap_preface.sh|86|68|Global Definitions|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  |bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Global Definitions:
bootstrap_preface.sh|87|69|Global Definitions|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|These globals describe the runtime environment and provide shared values used by|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Global Definitions:
bootstrap_preface.sh|88|70|Global Definitions|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|other framework components. They may include resolved paths, script metadata,|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Global Definitions:
bootstrap_preface.sh|89|71|Global Definitions|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|runtime flags, configuration locations, and other common settings.|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Global Definitions:
bootstrap_preface.sh|90|72|Global Definitions|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  |bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Global Definitions:
bootstrap_preface.sh|91|73|Global Definitions|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Configurable values are described through the current scoped registries. Framework|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Global Definitions:
bootstrap_preface.sh|92|74|Global Definitions|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|settings use|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Global Definitions:
bootstrap_preface.sh|93|75|Global Definitions|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|`SGND_FRAMEWORK_GLOBALS`; application settings use `SGND_SCRIPT_GLOBALS`; runtime|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Global Definitions:
bootstrap_preface.sh|94|76|Global Definitions|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|definitions and defaults are supplied by the bootstrap/environment layer.|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Global Definitions:
bootstrap_preface.sh|95|77|Global Definitions|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody||bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Global Definitions:
bootstrap_preface.sh|96|78|Global Definitions|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|These registries bridge static defaults, system/user configuration files, runtime|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Global Definitions:
bootstrap_preface.sh|97|79|Global Definitions|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|state, and command-line overrides without requiring each executable to implement|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Global Definitions:
bootstrap_preface.sh|98|80|Global Definitions|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|its own configuration model.|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Global Definitions:
bootstrap_preface.sh|99|81|Global Definitions|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody||bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Global Definitions:
