bootstrap_preface.sh|115|97|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionheader|Transferable Framework State|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|116|98|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody||bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|117|99|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Every executable bootstraps its own SolidGroundUX framework instance. Ordinary|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|118|100|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|shell globals therefore remain local to that process and are not automatically|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|119|101|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|shared with executables started from it.|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|120|102|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  |bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|121|103|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|SolidGroundUX preserves selected user-level runtime choices through a transferable|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|122|104|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|framework state file. The file is identified by `SGND_FRAMEWORK_STATEFILE` and is|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|123|105|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|normally resolved as:|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|124|106|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  |bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|125|107|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|    $SGND_USRCFG_DIR/framework.state|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|126|108|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  |bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|127|109|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|After the normal framework configuration has been loaded, bootstrap recalculates|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|128|110|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|this filename from the effective user configuration directory. If the file exists,|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|129|111|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|the variables listed in `SGND_FRAMEWORK_STATE` are loaded from it. If it does not|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|130|112|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|exist, bootstrap creates it from the current effective values.|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|131|113|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  |bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|132|114|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|The framework state is applied before the UI palette and style are loaded. This|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|133|115|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|allows a theme or logging choice changed by one SolidGroundUX executable to be used|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|134|116|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|by subsequently started executables, even though each executable creates its own|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|135|117|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|framework instance.|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|136|118|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  |bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|137|119|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Only explicitly listed variables are transferable. Process-specific values such as|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|138|120|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|script metadata, progress state, start times, and application-local state remain|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|139|121|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|private to the current executable. The framework state file is therefore a small|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|140|122|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|runtime overlay, not a dump of all framework globals and not a replacement for the|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|141|123|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|normal system and user configuration files.|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|142|124|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  |bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|143|125|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|The current transferable set is maintained in `SGND_FRAMEWORK_STATE` and includes|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|144|126|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|the active console and file log levels, UI style and palette, and the date format|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|145|127|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|used by `say()` output. Runtime functions that change one of these settings should|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|146|128|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|update the framework state file when the change must remain visible to later|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|147|129|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|framework instances.|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
bootstrap_preface.sh|148|130|Transferable Framework State|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody||bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Transferable Framework State:
