bootstrap_preface.sh|151|133|Console and File Log Levels|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Console output and logfile output are controlled independently.|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Console and File Log Levels:
bootstrap_preface.sh|152|134|Console and File Log Levels|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  |bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Console and File Log Levels:
bootstrap_preface.sh|153|135|Console and File Log Levels|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|`SGND_CONSOLE_LOG_LEVEL` controls which `say()` messages are rendered to the|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Console and File Log Levels:
bootstrap_preface.sh|154|136|Console and File Log Levels|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|terminal. `SGND_FILE_LOG_LEVEL` controls which messages are appended to the|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Console and File Log Levels:
bootstrap_preface.sh|155|137|Console and File Log Levels|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|resolved logfile. Both settings support the levels:|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Console and File Log Levels:
bootstrap_preface.sh|156|138|Console and File Log Levels|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  |bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Console and File Log Levels:
bootstrap_preface.sh|157|139|Console and File Log Levels|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|    silent, quiet, normal, verbose, debug, trace|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Console and File Log Levels:
bootstrap_preface.sh|158|140|Console and File Log Levels|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  |bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Console and File Log Levels:
bootstrap_preface.sh|159|141|Console and File Log Levels|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|A message can therefore be suppressed on screen while still being recorded in the|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Console and File Log Levels:
bootstrap_preface.sh|160|142|Console and File Log Levels|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|logfile, or displayed on screen while file logging is effectively disabled. Setting|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Console and File Log Levels:
bootstrap_preface.sh|161|143|Console and File Log Levels|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|`SGND_FILE_LOG_LEVEL` to `silent` disables logfile output without requiring a|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Console and File Log Levels:
bootstrap_preface.sh|162|144|Console and File Log Levels|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|separate enable flag.|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Console and File Log Levels:
bootstrap_preface.sh|163|145|Console and File Log Levels|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  |bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Console and File Log Levels:
bootstrap_preface.sh|164|146|Console and File Log Levels|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|`say()` evaluates the console and file thresholds separately. Matching logfile|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Console and File Log Levels:
bootstrap_preface.sh|165|147|Console and File Log Levels|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|entries are always written with a date/time prefix using `SAY_DATE_FORMAT`,|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Console and File Log Levels:
bootstrap_preface.sh|166|148|Console and File Log Levels|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|regardless of whether timestamps are currently shown on the console.|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Console and File Log Levels:
bootstrap_preface.sh|167|149|Console and File Log Levels|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  |bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Console and File Log Levels:
bootstrap_preface.sh|168|150|Console and File Log Levels|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|The active log levels are part of `SGND_FRAMEWORK_STATE`, so changes saved during|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Console and File Log Levels:
bootstrap_preface.sh|169|151|Console and File Log Levels|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|one framework instance become the starting values for later SolidGroundUX|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Console and File Log Levels:
bootstrap_preface.sh|170|152|Console and File Log Levels|Bootstrap||normal|||L2Sectionbody|executables run by the same user.|bootstrap_preface.sh::Bootstrap:Console and File Log Levels:
