ui_preface.sh|2|1||||normal|||moduleheader|SolidGroundUX - UI Framework|ui_preface.sh::::
ui_preface.sh|20|2|User Interface|||normal|||L1Sectionheader|User Interface|ui_preface.sh:::User Interface:
ui_preface.sh|21|3|User Interface|||normal|||L1Sectionbody||ui_preface.sh:::User Interface:
ui_preface.sh|22|4|User Interface|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|The SolidGroundUX user-interface layer provides a consistent vocabulary for|ui_preface.sh:::User Interface:
ui_preface.sh|23|5|User Interface|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|terminal output and interaction. It separates what an application wants to|ui_preface.sh:::User Interface:
ui_preface.sh|24|6|User Interface|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|communicate from the details of ANSI styling, terminal width, glyph selection,|ui_preface.sh:::User Interface:
ui_preface.sh|25|7|User Interface|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|prompt handling, and output policy.|ui_preface.sh:::User Interface:
ui_preface.sh|26|8|User Interface|||normal|||L1Sectionbody||ui_preface.sh:::User Interface:
ui_preface.sh|27|9|User Interface|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|Applications should normally use the public UI functions rather than assembling|ui_preface.sh:::User Interface:
ui_preface.sh|28|10|User Interface|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|escape sequences, labels, prompts, or status messages themselves. This keeps|ui_preface.sh:::User Interface:
ui_preface.sh|29|11|User Interface|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|scripts visually consistent and allows presentation rules to evolve without|ui_preface.sh:::User Interface:
ui_preface.sh|30|12|User Interface|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|requiring application code to be rewritten.|ui_preface.sh:::User Interface:
ui_preface.sh|31|13|User Interface|||normal|||L1Sectionbody||ui_preface.sh:::User Interface:
ui_preface.sh|32|14|UI Architecture|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionheader|UI Architecture|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:UI Architecture:
