ui_preface.sh|58|40|Rendering and Layout|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|The rendering layer in `ui.sh` provides reusable functions for structured console|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Rendering and Layout:
ui_preface.sh|59|41|Rendering and Layout|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|output. It handles visible string length, ANSI-aware padding, terminal width,|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Rendering and Layout:
ui_preface.sh|60|42|Rendering and Layout|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|themes, foreground and background colors, text attributes, title bars, section|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Rendering and Layout:
ui_preface.sh|61|43|Rendering and Layout|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|headers, filled lines, labeled values, and formatted cells.|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Rendering and Layout:
ui_preface.sh|62|44|Rendering and Layout|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody||ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Rendering and Layout:
ui_preface.sh|63|45|Rendering and Layout|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Width-sensitive functions use visible character length rather than raw byte|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Rendering and Layout:
ui_preface.sh|64|46|Rendering and Layout|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|length wherever possible. ANSI control sequences therefore do not disturb label|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Rendering and Layout:
ui_preface.sh|65|47|Rendering and Layout|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|alignment or layout calculations.|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Rendering and Layout:
