ui_preface.sh|96|78|Messages and Logging|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionheader|Messages and Logging|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Messages and Logging:
ui_preface.sh|97|79|Messages and Logging|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody||ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Messages and Logging:
ui_preface.sh|98|80|Messages and Logging|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|The messaging layer in `ui-say.sh` provides the standard way for scripts to emit|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Messages and Logging:
ui_preface.sh|99|81|Messages and Logging|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|informational, successful, warning, error, debug, and progress-related messages.|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Messages and Logging:
ui_preface.sh|100|82|Messages and Logging|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Message type, log level, console visibility, and optional file logging are handled|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Messages and Logging:
ui_preface.sh|101|83|Messages and Logging|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|independently from the application logic that produced the message.|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Messages and Logging:
ui_preface.sh|102|84|Messages and Logging|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody||ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Messages and Logging:
ui_preface.sh|103|85|Messages and Logging|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|This distinction is important: an application chooses the meaning and severity of|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Messages and Logging:
ui_preface.sh|104|86|Messages and Logging|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|a message, while the framework decides whether and how that message is displayed|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Messages and Logging:
ui_preface.sh|105|87|Messages and Logging|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|or recorded.|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Messages and Logging:
ui_preface.sh|106|88|Messages and Logging|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody||ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Messages and Logging:
ui_preface.sh|107|89|Messages and Logging|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Scripts should therefore use the `say` family consistently instead of mixing|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Messages and Logging:
ui_preface.sh|108|90|Messages and Logging|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|direct output with framework messages. Direct `printf` remains appropriate for|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Messages and Logging:
ui_preface.sh|109|91|Messages and Logging|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|machine-readable output or for narrowly controlled rendering inside the UI|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Messages and Logging:
ui_preface.sh|110|92|Messages and Logging|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|implementation itself.|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Messages and Logging:
ui_preface.sh|111|93|Messages and Logging|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody||ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Messages and Logging:
ui_preface.sh|112|94|Prompts and User Input|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionheader|Prompts and User Input|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Prompts and User Input:
ui_preface.sh|113|95|Prompts and User Input|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody||ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Prompts and User Input:
ui_preface.sh|114|96|Prompts and User Input|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|The prompt layer in `ui-ask.sh` provides interactive input without assuming that|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Prompts and User Input:
ui_preface.sh|115|97|Prompts and User Input|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|standard input is available. Where necessary, prompts read from the controlling|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Prompts and User Input:
ui_preface.sh|116|98|Prompts and User Input|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|terminal so that applications can still process redirected or piped input.|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Prompts and User Input:
ui_preface.sh|117|99|Prompts and User Input|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody||ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Prompts and User Input:
ui_preface.sh|118|100|Prompts and User Input|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|The public prompt API supports labeled input, editable defaults, validation,|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Prompts and User Input:
ui_preface.sh|119|101|Prompts and User Input|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|constrained decisions, timed continuation, immediate key choices, and small|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Prompts and User Input:
ui_preface.sh|120|102|Prompts and User Input|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|field-driven forms.|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Prompts and User Input:
ui_preface.sh|121|103|Prompts and User Input|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody||ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Prompts and User Input:
ui_preface.sh|122|104|Prompts and User Input|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Principal functions include:|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Prompts and User Input:
