ui_preface.sh|126|108|Prompts and User Input|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|    ask_dlg_autocontinue|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Prompts and User Input:
ui_preface.sh|127|109|Prompts and User Input|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|    ask_choose|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Prompts and User Input:
ui_preface.sh|128|110|Prompts and User Input|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|    ask_choose_immediate|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Prompts and User Input:
ui_preface.sh|129|111|Prompts and User Input|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|    ask_prompt_form|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Prompts and User Input:
ui_preface.sh|130|112|Prompts and User Input|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody||ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Prompts and User Input:
ui_preface.sh|131|113|Prompts and User Input|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Prompt functions normalize common interaction patterns so applications do not|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Prompts and User Input:
ui_preface.sh|132|114|Prompts and User Input|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|need to reproduce terminal handling, label formatting, default-value behavior, or|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Prompts and User Input:
ui_preface.sh|133|115|Prompts and User Input|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|response validation.|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Prompts and User Input:
ui_preface.sh|134|116|Prompts and User Input|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody||ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Prompts and User Input:
ui_preface.sh|135|117|Prompts and User Input|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Use `ask_decision` for an explicit user decision that should block until a choice is|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Prompts and User Input:
ui_preface.sh|136|118|Prompts and User Input|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|made. Use `ask_dlg_autocontinue` for an interruptible timed continuation where the|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Prompts and User Input:
ui_preface.sh|137|119|Prompts and User Input|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|normal path continues automatically but the operator may intervene, pause, redo, or|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Prompts and User Input:
ui_preface.sh|138|120|Prompts and User Input|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|cancel according to the options supplied. These are distinct interaction patterns.|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Prompts and User Input:
ui_preface.sh|139|121|Prompts and User Input|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody||ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Prompts and User Input:
ui_preface.sh|140|122|Dialog-Oriented Interaction|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionheader|Dialog-Oriented Interaction|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Dialog-Oriented Interaction:
ui_preface.sh|141|123|Dialog-Oriented Interaction|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody||ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Dialog-Oriented Interaction:
ui_preface.sh|142|124|Dialog-Oriented Interaction|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|The dialog layer in `ui-dlg.sh` builds structured decisions on top of the lower|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Dialog-Oriented Interaction:
ui_preface.sh|143|125|Dialog-Oriented Interaction|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|prompt primitives. It expands symbolic choices, displays available actions,|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Dialog-Oriented Interaction:
ui_preface.sh|144|126|Dialog-Oriented Interaction|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|normalizes keyboard input, translates dialog return codes, and supports timed|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Dialog-Oriented Interaction:
ui_preface.sh|145|127|Dialog-Oriented Interaction|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|auto-continue behavior.|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Dialog-Oriented Interaction:
ui_preface.sh|146|128|Dialog-Oriented Interaction|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody||ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Dialog-Oriented Interaction:
ui_preface.sh|147|129|Dialog-Oriented Interaction|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|These helpers are intentionally lightweight. They provide predictable interaction|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Dialog-Oriented Interaction:
ui_preface.sh|148|130|Dialog-Oriented Interaction|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|patterns for shell applications without introducing a full-screen terminal user|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Dialog-Oriented Interaction:
ui_preface.sh|149|131|Dialog-Oriented Interaction|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|interface or a separate workflow engine.|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Dialog-Oriented Interaction:
ui_preface.sh|150|132|Dialog-Oriented Interaction|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody||ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Dialog-Oriented Interaction:
ui_preface.sh|151|133|Glyphs and Character Fallbacks|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionheader|Glyphs and Character Fallbacks|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Glyphs and Character Fallbacks:
ui_preface.sh|152|134|Glyphs and Character Fallbacks|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody||ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Glyphs and Character Fallbacks:
ui_preface.sh|153|135|Glyphs and Character Fallbacks|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|`ui-glyphs.sh` centralizes the visual symbols used throughout the framework.|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Glyphs and Character Fallbacks:
ui_preface.sh|154|136|Glyphs and Character Fallbacks|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Keeping glyphs in one place avoids repeated literal Unicode characters and makes|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Glyphs and Character Fallbacks:
ui_preface.sh|155|137|Glyphs and Character Fallbacks|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|it possible to provide simpler fallbacks for restricted terminals.|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Glyphs and Character Fallbacks:
ui_preface.sh|156|138|Glyphs and Character Fallbacks|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody||ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Glyphs and Character Fallbacks:
ui_preface.sh|157|139|Glyphs and Character Fallbacks|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Rendering code should refer to the shared glyph definitions rather than choosing|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Glyphs and Character Fallbacks:
ui_preface.sh|158|140|Glyphs and Character Fallbacks|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|local arrows, checkmarks, separators, or box-drawing characters. This preserves a|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Glyphs and Character Fallbacks:
ui_preface.sh|159|141|Glyphs and Character Fallbacks|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|recognizable visual language across the framework.|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Glyphs and Character Fallbacks:
ui_preface.sh|160|142|Glyphs and Character Fallbacks|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody||ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Glyphs and Character Fallbacks:
ui_preface.sh|161|143|Rendering Width and Message Routing|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionheader|Rendering Width and Message Routing|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Rendering Width and Message Routing:
ui_preface.sh|162|144|Rendering Width and Message Routing|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody||ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Rendering Width and Message Routing:
ui_preface.sh|163|145|Rendering Width and Message Routing|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Width-aware UI primitives derive their default width from the active terminal. An|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Rendering Width and Message Routing:
ui_preface.sh|164|146|Rendering Width and Message Routing|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|explicit `--maxwidth` is honored when supplied, and `SGND_MAX_RENDER_WIDTH` acts as|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Rendering Width and Message Routing:
ui_preface.sh|165|147|Rendering Width and Message Routing|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|an optional global cap; an unset or zero cap allows use of the full terminal width.|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Rendering Width and Message Routing:
ui_preface.sh|166|148|Rendering Width and Message Routing|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody||ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Rendering Width and Message Routing:
ui_preface.sh|167|149|Rendering Width and Message Routing|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|The `say*` family routes semantic messages independently to console and file output.|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Rendering Width and Message Routing:
ui_preface.sh|168|150|Rendering Width and Message Routing|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|`SGND_CONSOLE_LOG_LEVEL` controls terminal visibility and `SGND_FILE_LOG_LEVEL`|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Rendering Width and Message Routing:
ui_preface.sh|169|151|Rendering Width and Message Routing|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|controls persistent logging, allowing the two audiences to use different detail|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Rendering Width and Message Routing:
