ui_preface.sh|173|155|Guidance for Applications|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody||ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Guidance for Applications:
ui_preface.sh|174|156|Guidance for Applications|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|A SolidGroundUX application should generally follow these rules:|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Guidance for Applications:
ui_preface.sh|175|157|Guidance for Applications|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody||ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Guidance for Applications:
ui_preface.sh|176|158|Guidance for Applications|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|    - Use `say` functions for user-facing status and diagnostic messages.|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Guidance for Applications:
ui_preface.sh|177|159|Guidance for Applications|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|    - Use rendering helpers for standard titles, sections, labels, and tables.|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Guidance for Applications:
ui_preface.sh|178|160|Guidance for Applications|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|    - Use prompt and dialog helpers for interactive decisions.|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Guidance for Applications:
ui_preface.sh|179|161|Guidance for Applications|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|    - Do not embed ANSI escape sequences in application code.|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Guidance for Applications:
ui_preface.sh|180|162|Guidance for Applications|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|    - Do not duplicate glyphs or terminal-width calculations locally.|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Guidance for Applications:
ui_preface.sh|181|163|Guidance for Applications|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|    - Keep machine-readable output separate from styled human-readable output.|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Guidance for Applications:
ui_preface.sh|182|164|Guidance for Applications|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|    - Respect non-interactive, quiet, debug, and dry-run execution modes.|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Guidance for Applications:
ui_preface.sh|183|165|Guidance for Applications|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody||ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Guidance for Applications:
ui_preface.sh|184|166|Guidance for Applications|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Following these conventions gives command-line tools a shared appearance and,|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Guidance for Applications:
ui_preface.sh|185|167|Guidance for Applications|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|more importantly, shared behavior. Users can learn one interaction model and|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Guidance for Applications:
ui_preface.sh|186|168|Guidance for Applications|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|apply it across all SolidGroundUX applications.|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Guidance for Applications:
ui_preface.sh|187|169|Guidance for Applications|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody||ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Guidance for Applications:
ui_preface.sh|188|170|Scope and Non-Goals|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionheader|Scope and Non-Goals|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Scope and Non-Goals:
ui_preface.sh|189|171|Scope and Non-Goals|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody||ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Scope and Non-Goals:
ui_preface.sh|190|172|Scope and Non-Goals|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|The UI framework is designed for structured command-line applications. It is not|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Scope and Non-Goals:
ui_preface.sh|191|173|Scope and Non-Goals|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|intended to be a full-screen TUI toolkit, a graphical interface, or a replacement|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Scope and Non-Goals:
ui_preface.sh|192|174|Scope and Non-Goals|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|for dedicated terminal-layout libraries.|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Scope and Non-Goals:
ui_preface.sh|193|175|Scope and Non-Goals|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody||ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Scope and Non-Goals:
ui_preface.sh|194|176|Scope and Non-Goals|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Its goal is deliberately narrower: provide dependable, composable primitives for|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Scope and Non-Goals:
ui_preface.sh|195|177|Scope and Non-Goals|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|readable output, consistent messaging, and predictable interaction in Bash.|ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Scope and Non-Goals:
ui-glyphs.sh|2|1||||normal|||moduleheader|SolidGroundUX - UI Glyphs|ui-glyphs.sh::::
ui-glyphs.sh|13|2||||label|||modulebody|Description|ui-glyphs.sh::::
ui-glyphs.sh|14|3||||normal|||modulebody|  Defines reusable glyphs, symbols, and character helpers for use in|ui-glyphs.sh::::
ui-glyphs.sh|15|4||||normal|||modulebody|  console output across the SolidGroundUX framework.|ui-glyphs.sh::::
ui-glyphs.sh|16|5||||normal|||modulebody||ui-glyphs.sh::::
ui-glyphs.sh|17|6||||label|||modulebody|The library|ui-glyphs.sh::::
ui-glyphs.sh|18|7||||normal|||modulebody|    - Provides box-drawing characters and layout elements|ui-glyphs.sh::::
ui-glyphs.sh|19|8||||normal|||modulebody|    - Defines commonly used symbols (checkmarks, arrows, separators, etc.)|ui-glyphs.sh::::
ui-glyphs.sh|20|9||||normal|||modulebody|    - Encapsulates Unicode and ASCII fallbacks where needed|ui-glyphs.sh::::
ui-glyphs.sh|21|10||||normal|||modulebody|    - Supports consistent visual language across all UI components|ui-glyphs.sh::::
ui-glyphs.sh|22|11||||normal|||modulebody||ui-glyphs.sh::::
ui-glyphs.sh|23|12||||label|||modulebody|Design principles|ui-glyphs.sh::::
ui-glyphs.sh|24|13||||normal|||modulebody|  - Centralize glyph definitions to avoid duplication|ui-glyphs.sh::::
ui-glyphs.sh|25|14||||normal|||modulebody|  - Prefer readability and consistency over decorative complexity|ui-glyphs.sh::::
ui-glyphs.sh|26|15||||normal|||modulebody|  - Allow graceful fallback for terminals with limited Unicode support|ui-glyphs.sh::::
ui-glyphs.sh|27|16||||normal|||modulebody|  - Keep rendering concerns separate from glyph definition|ui-glyphs.sh::::
ui-glyphs.sh|28|17||||normal|||modulebody||ui-glyphs.sh::::
ui-glyphs.sh|29|18||||label|||modulebody|Role in framework|ui-glyphs.sh::::
ui-glyphs.sh|30|19||||normal|||modulebody|  - Foundational visual layer used by ui.sh and related UI modules|ui-glyphs.sh::::
ui-glyphs.sh|31|20||||normal|||modulebody|  - Supports consistent styling across all console tools|ui-glyphs.sh::::
ui-glyphs.sh|32|21||||normal|||modulebody||ui-glyphs.sh::::
ui-glyphs.sh|33|22||||label|||modulebody|Non-goals|ui-glyphs.sh::::
ui-glyphs.sh|34|23||||normal|||modulebody|  - Rendering logic or layout behavior|ui-glyphs.sh::::
ui-glyphs.sh|35|24||||normal|||modulebody|  - Terminal capability detection beyond basic fallback handling|ui-glyphs.sh::::
ui-glyphs.sh|36|25||||normal|||modulebody|  - Theme or color management|ui-glyphs.sh::::
ui-glyphs.sh|37|26||||normal|||modulebody||ui-glyphs.sh::::
