solidgroundux_preface.sh|22|3|How it came to pass...|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|During a period in which I found myself lacking mental challenges in my current project, I decided to explore|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::How it came to pass...:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|23|4|How it came to pass...|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|the Linux world. Frustrated with the current software market, I envisioned creating a subscription-free,|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::How it came to pass...:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|24|5|How it came to pass...|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|vendor-neutral, on-site software solution. This started with configuring a few VMs, which quickly led to|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::How it came to pass...:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|25|6|How it came to pass...|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|needing to learn Bash. I received a lot of help with syntax from ChatGPT, but I quickly concluded that I|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::How it came to pass...:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|26|7|How it came to pass...|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|didn't want to have to type printf, read, and other boilerplate every time I wanted to communicate with|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::How it came to pass...:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|27|8|How it came to pass...|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|the user or request input.|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::How it came to pass...:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|28|9|How it came to pass...|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|  |solidgroundux_preface.sh:::How it came to pass...:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|29|10|How it came to pass...|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|Coming from the C#/.NET ecosystem required some adjustment, especially letting go of object-oriented|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::How it came to pass...:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|30|11|How it came to pass...|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|thinking. Even so, I found myself constantly looking for ways to make things more modular, reusable,|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::How it came to pass...:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|31|12|How it came to pass...|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|and consistent.|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::How it came to pass...:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|32|13|How it came to pass...|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|  |solidgroundux_preface.sh:::How it came to pass...:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|33|14|How it came to pass...|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|To make a long story short, six months later I present to you SolidGroundUX: a modular, reusable,|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::How it came to pass...:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|34|15|How it came to pass...|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|consistent, and hopefully enjoyable framework for building console applications in Bash. Not bad for a|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::How it came to pass...:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|35|16|How it came to pass...|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|first Bash project. I haven't configured a single VM since I started building it, so I sometimes wonder|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::How it came to pass...:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|36|17|How it came to pass...|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|whether the original plan still works...|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::How it came to pass...:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|37|18|How it came to pass...|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|  |solidgroundux_preface.sh:::How it came to pass...:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|38|19|How it came to pass...|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|I'm releasing this software on GitHub under the Testadura Non-Commercial License (TD-NC) v1.1. This means|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::How it came to pass...:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|39|20|How it came to pass...|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|you can use it free of charge for non-commercial purposes, even within a commercial environment. However,|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::How it came to pass...:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|40|21|How it came to pass...|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|if you wish to use it as part of a commercial product or project, we will need to discuss licensing terms.|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::How it came to pass...:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|41|22|How it came to pass...|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|  |solidgroundux_preface.sh:::How it came to pass...:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|42|23|How it came to pass...|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|I hope this framework makes someone's life a little easier. If you have suggestions for improvements,|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::How it came to pass...:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|43|24|How it came to pass...|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|discover a bug, or would like to contribute, feel free to reach out.|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::How it came to pass...:
