solidgroundux_preface.sh|47|28|How it came to pass...|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|The name SolidGround originates from a .NET ETL orchestration framework that I have been developing over|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::How it came to pass...:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|48|29|How it came to pass...|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|the past ten years. That product is currently awaiting its adaptation to Linux and the Avalonia UI|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::How it came to pass...:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|49|30|How it came to pass...|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|framework, after which it is intended to be released as a commercial product in the hopefully near future.|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::How it came to pass...:
