solidgroundux_preface.sh|231|211|Architecture|||normal|||L1Sectionheader|Architecture|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|232|212|Architecture|||normal|||L1Sectionbody||solidgroundux_preface.sh:::Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|233|213|Architecture|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|SolidGroundUX is designed as a framework rather than a collection of unrelated|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|234|214|Architecture|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|helper scripts. The goal is to provide a consistent and reusable foundation for|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|235|215|Architecture|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|building structured Bash applications while minimizing repetitive boilerplate.|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|236|216|Architecture|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|  |solidgroundux_preface.sh:::Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|237|217|Architecture|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|Although implemented entirely in Bash, many of the architectural principles are|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|238|218|Architecture|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|inspired by modern application frameworks. Concepts such as separation of concerns,|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|239|219|Architecture|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|modularity, convention over configuration, documentation-driven development, and|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|240|220|Architecture|||normal|||L1Sectionbody|reusable components are applied throughout the framework.|solidgroundux_preface.sh:::Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|241|221|Architecture|||normal|||L1Sectionbody||solidgroundux_preface.sh:::Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|242|222|Layered Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionheader|Layered Architecture|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Layered Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|243|223|Layered Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody||solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Layered Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|244|224|Layered Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|The framework is organized into several logical layers.|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Layered Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|245|225|Layered Architecture|Architecture||highlight|||L2Sectionbody|Images|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Layered Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|246|226|Layered Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  Framework-Architecture.png :: Figure 1 – SolidGroundUX layered architecture.  |solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Layered Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|247|227|Layered Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody||solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Layered Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|248|228|Layered Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|The diagram provides a high-level overview of the major framework|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Layered Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|249|229|Layered Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|components and their relationships. The remainder of this documentation|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Layered Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|250|230|Layered Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|explores each layer and subsystem in greater detail.|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Layered Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|251|231|Layered Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody||solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Layered Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|252|232|Layered Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|At the foundation are the core libraries. These provide reusable functionality|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Layered Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|253|233|Layered Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|such as configuration management, state handling, command-line argument processing,|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Layered Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|254|234|Layered Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|user interaction, metadata handling, logging, deployment support, and|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Layered Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|255|235|Layered Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|documentation generation.|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Layered Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|256|236|Layered Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  |solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Layered Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|257|237|Layered Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Above the library layer are executable applications. These are standalone tools|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Layered Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|258|238|Layered Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|such as workspace generators, deployment utilities, release preparation, wrapper|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Layered Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|259|239|Layered Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|generation, release management, and documentation generators.|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Layered Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|260|240|Layered Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  |solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Layered Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|261|241|Layered Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|The framework also supports modular console applications. Independent modules can|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Layered Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|262|242|Layered Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|register menu groups and menu items with a common host application, providing a|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Layered Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|263|243|Layered Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|lightweight plugin architecture implemented entirely in Bash.|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Layered Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|264|244|Layered Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody||solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Layered Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|265|245|Bootstrap Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionheader|Bootstrap Architecture|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Bootstrap Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|266|246|Bootstrap Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody||solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Bootstrap Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|267|247|Bootstrap Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|The bootstrap system is the heart of the framework.|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Bootstrap Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|268|248|Bootstrap Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  |solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Bootstrap Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|269|249|Bootstrap Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Rather than requiring every script to discover filesystem locations, load|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Bootstrap Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|270|250|Bootstrap Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|libraries, initialize configuration, and prepare runtime variables independently,|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Bootstrap Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|271|251|Bootstrap Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|the bootstrap libraries provide a standardized initialization sequence.|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Bootstrap Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|272|252|Bootstrap Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  |solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Bootstrap Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|273|253|Bootstrap Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|A typical startup sequence consists of:|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Bootstrap Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|274|254|Bootstrap Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  |solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Bootstrap Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|275|255|Bootstrap Architecture|Architecture||highlight|||L2Sectionbody|Images|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Bootstrap Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|276|256|Bootstrap Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  Bootstrap-Sequence.png :: Figure 3 – SolidGroundUX bootstrap sequence.  |solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Bootstrap Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|277|257|Bootstrap Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody||solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Bootstrap Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|278|258|Bootstrap Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  |solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Bootstrap Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|279|259|Bootstrap Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|By centralizing initialization logic, application scripts remain focused on their|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Bootstrap Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|280|260|Bootstrap Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|actual purpose rather than infrastructure concerns.|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Bootstrap Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|281|261|Bootstrap Architecture|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody||solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Bootstrap Architecture:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|282|262|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionheader|Public and Internal APIs|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|283|263|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody||solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|284|264|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|SolidGroundUX uses naming conventions to distinguish public APIs from internal|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|285|265|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|implementation details.|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|286|266|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  |solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|287|267|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Public framework functions use `sgnd_*` and are intended for application and tool|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|288|268|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|consumers.|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|289|269|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody||solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|290|270|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Framework-internal functions use `_sgnd_*`. They are effectively protected: other|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|291|271|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|cooperating SolidGroundUX libraries may depend on them, but they are not part of|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|292|272|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|the supported application-facing API.|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|293|273|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody||solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|294|274|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Plain leading-underscore helpers such as `_helper` are local/private implementation|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|295|275|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|details belonging to one script or module. Bash cannot enforce these access levels,|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|296|276|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|but the convention communicates intended ownership. Consumers should rely on the|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|297|277|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|public `sgnd_*` surface unless they are implementing framework internals.|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|298|278|Public and Internal APIs|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody||solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Public and Internal APIs:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|299|279|Convention Over Configuration|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionheader|Convention Over Configuration|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Convention Over Configuration:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|300|280|Convention Over Configuration|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody||solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Convention Over Configuration:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|301|281|Convention Over Configuration|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|One of the primary design goals of SolidGroundUX is reducing repetitive code.|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Convention Over Configuration:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|302|282|Convention Over Configuration|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  |solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Convention Over Configuration:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|303|283|Convention Over Configuration|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Common functionality such as argument processing, configuration loading, state|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Convention Over Configuration:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|304|284|Convention Over Configuration|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|management, user interaction, documentation generation, and deployment support|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Convention Over Configuration:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|305|285|Convention Over Configuration|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|are implemented once and reused throughout the framework.|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Convention Over Configuration:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|306|286|Convention Over Configuration|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  |solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Convention Over Configuration:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|307|287|Convention Over Configuration|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Developers remain free to override framework behavior when necessary, but most|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Convention Over Configuration:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|308|288|Convention Over Configuration|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|applications can rely on framework conventions and focus primarily on business|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Convention Over Configuration:
solidgroundux_preface.sh|309|289|Convention Over Configuration|Architecture||normal|||L2Sectionbody|logic.|solidgroundux_preface.sh::Architecture:Convention Over Configuration:
sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh|2|1||||normal|||moduleheader|SolidGroundUX - Bootstrap Environment|sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh::::
sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh|13|2||||label|||modulebody|Description|sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh::::
sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh|14|3||||normal|||modulebody|  Establishes the runtime environment for SolidGroundUX scripts.|sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh::::
sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh|15|4||||normal|||modulebody||sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh::::
sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh|16|5||||label|||modulebody|The library|sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh::::
sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh|17|6||||normal|||modulebody|    - Defines and initializes core framework directories|sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh::::
sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh|18|7||||normal|||modulebody|    - Resolves system and user paths (config, state, logs, etc.)|sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh::::
sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh|19|8||||normal|||modulebody|    - Ensures required directories exist with proper permissions|sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh::::
sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh|20|9||||normal|||modulebody|    - Applies default values for environment variables when unset|sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh::::
sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh|21|10||||normal|||modulebody|    - Normalizes environment behavior across different execution contexts|sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh::::
sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh|22|11||||normal|||modulebody||sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh::::
sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh|23|12||||label|||modulebody|Design principles|sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh::::
sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh|24|13||||normal|||modulebody|  - Deterministic environment setup regardless of execution context|sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh::::
sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh|25|14||||normal|||modulebody|  - A single self-locating framework root for all framework-managed filesystem paths|sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh::::
sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh|26|15||||normal|||modulebody|  - Safe defaults with minimal assumptions about host system|sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh::::
sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh|27|16||||normal|||modulebody|  - Idempotent setup (safe to run multiple times)|sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh::::
sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh|28|17||||normal|||modulebody||sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh::::
sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh|29|18||||label|||modulebody|Role in framework|sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh::::
sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh|30|19||||normal|||modulebody|  - Core bootstrap layer responsible for environment initialization|sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh::::
sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh|31|20||||normal|||modulebody|  - Runs early in the bootstrap process before other libraries depend on it|sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh::::
sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh|32|21||||normal|||modulebody|  - Provides foundational paths and variables used across all modules|sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh::::
sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh|33|22||||normal|||modulebody||sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh::::
sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh|34|23||||label|||modulebody|Non-goals|sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh::::
sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh|35|24||||normal|||modulebody|  - Argument parsing (handled by sgnd-args.sh)|sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh::::
sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh|36|25||||normal|||modulebody|  - Configuration loading (handled by sgnd-cfg.sh)|sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh::::
sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh|37|26||||normal|||modulebody|  - UI or user interaction|sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh::::
sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh|38|27||||normal|||modulebody||sgnd-bootstrap-env.sh::::
